 "notes": "East side of the Col de Peyresourde from Bagnères-de-Luchon (app: start 625 m, 13.7 km; Saint-Aventin km 5.2, Castillon 6.5, Garin 8.0). km 0 = Place du Comminges in the centre of Luchon (north end of Avenue Carnot), from where the route takes Rue Nérée Boubée for 200 m to the start of the D618 (Avenue Jean Moulin); this foot reproduces the app length (routed 13.69 km) and village positions (Saint-Aventin 5.2, Castillon 6.2, Garin 7.6). Route: D618 only — out of Luchon on Avenue Jean Moulin, Payssas, the flat section below Trébons, two hairpins at the junction with the Vallée d'Oueil road (Port de Balès), Saint-Aventin, below Castillon- and Cazeaux-de-Larboust, Garin, then the long open drag and three final hairpins to the col. The summit is the high point of the D618 (DEM ~1570 m), ~300 m before the roundabout where the Peyragudes road branches off (the Wikipedia/Geohack point 42.7969, 0.4533 lies on that Peyragudes road, not on the D618). Coordinates are on the Overture/OSM road geometry; km are routed distances from the foot. Note: in the Tour 2021 (stage 17) the race entered Luchon from the D125 and its itinerary gives Luchon→col 15.7 km with Saint-Aventin at 6.7 km — a different start inside Luchon, not used here.",
